---
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="File a Bug Report - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="file-bug-report">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="The agent can investigate a flaky outside API and turn what it finds into a bug report the vendor can act on.">
			Kaiju watch data in the portals comes from Tidewatch, an outside monitoring feed that the API syncs on a timer. The sync
			fails now and then, and Tidewatch won't look into it without details.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message kind="email" subject="Tidewatch keeps failing" from="Platform Engineer" to="Web Team" date="Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:05">
			<p>
				The API log shows the Tidewatch sync failing every so often. It's not every time, and the portals keep working off the
				last copy, but the forecasts go stale.
			</p>
			<p>
				I raised it with Tidewatch support and they said they need specifics before they can investigate. Can you put together a
				report for them? Assume their engineers will read it, not support.
			</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent test the Tidewatch API, find out what's failing, and write an HTML bug report for the vendor.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Check what the API log already records about failed syncs.",
				"Call the Tidewatch API directly, enough times to measure how often it fails.",
				"Record the trace ID, timestamp, status code and response for each failure.",
				"Work out the failure rate, and which requests fail.",
				"Look for anything the failing responses have in common.",
				"Produce an HTML report Tidewatch's engineers could act on without asking follow-up questions.",
				"Leave our API key out of the report.",
			]}
		/>

		<Answer
			prompt={`Our API's sync with Tidewatch fails now and then, and Tidewatch needs details before they'll investigate.

Check our API log for failed syncs, then call the Tidewatch API directly, enough times on each endpoint to measure how often it fails. For every failure, record the trace ID, timestamp, status code, response body and all response headers, and look for anything the failing responses have in common.

Write an HTML report for Tidewatch's engineers with the failure rate, any pattern you find, and the trace IDs they need to look it up. Don't include our API key.`}
		>
			<p>
				Every Tidewatch response carries <code>X-Trace-Id</code> and <code>X-Served-By</code>. A good report lists trace IDs,
				timestamps, status codes and the failure rate from a run of repeated calls.
			</p>
			<p>
				A great one spots that every failure comes from <code>tw-node-03</code>, and only on <code>/v1/forecasts</code>, and quotes
				the <code>ensemble_desync</code> error. That tells the vendor where to look. The API log records trace IDs but not the
				node, so an agent that only reads the log can't find this. It has to call Tidewatch itself and compare the headers across
				many calls. A handful of calls isn't enough, because the failure rate is about one in ten.
			</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
